          "english_quote": "to whom else can anyone grant this, or even grant that it is capable of coming into being?",
          "issue": "The draft interprets the second object as justice itself being capable of coming into existence. A material alternative keeps τίνι governing both grants: to whom can one grant being just, or even the ability to become just? On that reading, the recipient is the implicit subject of the infinitives, and 'just' is understood from the preceding τὸ δικαίῳ εἶναι. The note supplies another paraphrase of the abstract-emergence reading, but neither preserves this recipient/capacity alternative nor explains the preference for justice as the implicit subject. This is an interpretive-disclosure problem, not source corruption.",
