          "source_quote": "(ὁ μὲν γὰρ παρὼν κόσμος πρόσκαιρος, ὁ δὲ ἐσόμενος ἀΐδιος.)",
          "english_quote": "(For the present world is temporary, but the coming age is eternal.)",
          "issue": "The second member prints no noun: ὁ δὲ ἐσόμενος means 'but the coming [one].' Supplying 'age' is contextually defensible from the preceding κόσμον, αἰῶνα, but the immediate balanced construction also naturally supplies κόσμος, yielding 'the world to come.' The draft silently selects 'age' and does not disclose or explain this material referent choice. Because the surrounding passage explicitly distinguishes and alternates κόσμος and αἰών, the source-transparent 'world' candidate requires comparison.",
